# Booking availability — /api/availability
#
# Without these the calendar shows the opening hours from src/lib/availability.ts
# and tells the visitor so. With them, busy time is subtracted from the real
# calendar and the visitor sees actual free slots.

# The calendar to read. A Google account's own calendar is its email address.
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=henrik@initconsulting.no

# --- Option A: act as the account itself (works on any Workspace policy) ---
# Made once with the OAuth playground or a local consent flow, scope:
#   https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# --- Option B: a service account ---
# Tidier, but only works if the calendar above can be SHARED with the service
# account address ("See all event details"). Some Workspace domains block
# sharing outside the organisation, which a service account counts as — if the
# server log shows "calendar not readable", that is what happened; use A.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
# The whole private key on one line, newlines written as \n.
GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Option A is used when all three of its variables are set; otherwise B.
